; An @external var read only by the audio thread: its audience has no main
; bit, so embedder writes flow to audio directly through the table — the
; main thread must never publish OR adopt it (no main- lines for `gain`
; may appear anywhere, bootstrap included: main's replica of a var outside
; its audience is never authoritative). The embedder seeds it before the
; run and retunes it mid-run; each audio batch adopts the newest value.
@external
(var gain: f32)

@audio
(defn f [t: f32
         rate: f32]: f32
  gain)

@cpu
(defn main []
  (spawn-window (fn []
                    (start-audio f))))
